{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function createKeyHold(key): () => boolean;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/solid-hotkeys/src/createKeyHold.ts#L46","children":[{"type":"text","value":"createKeyHold.ts:46"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SolidJS primitive that returns whether a specific key is currently being held."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This primitive uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useSelector"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/solid-store"},{"type":"text","value":" to subscribe\nto the global KeyStateTracker and uses a selector to determine if the\nspecified key is held."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"key","children":[{"type":"text","value":"key"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"IndividualKey"},{"type":"text","value":" | (() => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"IndividualKey"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The key to check (e.g., 'Shift', 'Control', 'A') - can be an accessor function"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Signal accessor that returns true if the key is currently held down"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"() => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function ShiftIndicator() {\n  const isShiftHeld = createKeyHold('Shift')\n\n  return (\n    <div style={{ opacity: isShiftHeld() ? 1 : 0.5 }}>\n      {isShiftHeld() ? 'Shift is pressed!' : 'Press Shift'}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"function ModifierIndicators() {\n  const ctrl = createKeyHold('Control')\n  const shift = createKeyHold('Shift')\n  const alt = createKeyHold('Alt')\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <span style={{ opacity: ctrl() ? 1 : 0.3 }}>Ctrl</span>\n      <span style={{ opacity: shift() ? 1 : 0.3 }}>Shift</span>\n      <span style={{ opacity: alt() ? 1 : 0.3 }}>Alt</span>\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"key","text":"key","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction createKeyHold(key): () => boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [createKeyHold.ts:46](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/solid-hotkeys/src/createKeyHold.ts#L46)\n\nSolidJS primitive that returns whether a specific key is currently being held.\n\nThis primitive uses `useSelector` from `@tanstack/solid-store` to subscribe\nto the global KeyStateTracker and uses a selector to determine if the\nspecified key is held.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### key\n\n`IndividualKey` \\| (() => `IndividualKey`)\n\nThe key to check (e.g., 'Shift', 'Control', 'A') - can be an accessor function\n\n## Returns\n\nSignal accessor that returns true if the key is currently held down\n\n() => `boolean`\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nfunction ShiftIndicator() {\n  const isShiftHeld = createKeyHold('Shift')\n\n  return (\n    <div style={{ opacity: isShiftHeld() ? 1 : 0.5 }}>\n      {isShiftHeld() ? 'Shift is pressed!' : 'Press Shift'}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\nfunction ModifierIndicators() {\n  const ctrl = createKeyHold('Control')\n  const shift = createKeyHold('Shift')\n  const alt = createKeyHold('Alt')\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <span style={{ opacity: ctrl() ? 1 : 0.3 }}>Ctrl</span>\n      <span style={{ opacity: shift() ? 1 : 0.3 }}>Shift</span>\n      <span style={{ opacity: alt() ? 1 : 0.3 }}>Alt</span>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: createKeyHold\ntitle: createKeyHold\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction createKeyHold(key): () => boolean;\n```\n\nDefined in: [createKeyHold.ts:46](https://github.com/TanStack/hotkeys/blob/main/packages/solid-hotkeys/src/createKeyHold.ts#L46)\n\nSolidJS primitive that returns whether a specific key is currently being held.\n\nThis primitive uses `useSelector` from `@tanstack/solid-store` to subscribe\nto the global KeyStateTracker and uses a selector to determine if the\nspecified key is held.\n\n## Parameters\n\n### key\n\n`IndividualKey` \\| (() => `IndividualKey`)\n\nThe key to check (e.g., 'Shift', 'Control', 'A') - can be an accessor function\n\n## Returns\n\nSignal accessor that returns true if the key is currently held down\n\n() => `boolean`\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nfunction ShiftIndicator() {\n  const isShiftHeld = createKeyHold('Shift')\n\n  return (\n    <div style={{ opacity: isShiftHeld() ? 1 : 0.5 }}>\n      {isShiftHeld() ? 'Shift is pressed!' : 'Press Shift'}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n```tsx\nfunction ModifierIndicators() {\n  const ctrl = createKeyHold('Control')\n  const shift = createKeyHold('Shift')\n  const alt = createKeyHold('Alt')\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      <span style={{ opacity: ctrl() ? 1 : 0.3 }}>Ctrl</span>\n      <span style={{ opacity: shift() ? 1 : 0.3 }}>Shift</span>\n      <span style={{ opacity: alt() ? 1 : 0.3 }}>Alt</span>\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n"}
